Two leftovers from #118, both deliberately not fixed there under the
surgical-changes rule -- they are pre-existing and would have meant rewriting
blocks nobody asked about.

1. Markup is inconsistent, and the agents matched the local majority rather
   than picking a side:
   - Config.pm: `statuses` and `default_config` use =method, the other 17
     pre-existing blocks use =head2. The seven new blocks followed =head2.
   - Role/BoardAccess.pm: the three pre-existing blocks (log_action, log_agent,
     log_task_write) use =head2; the nine new ones use =method.
   - BoardStore.pm is =head2 throughout, Task.pm and Git.pm are =method.

   CLAUDE.md names =attr/=method as the convention. Note this is cosmetic in
   the built dist: Pod::Elemental::Transformer::Author::GETTY turns =attr,
   =method and =func into =head2 alike, so nothing renders differently -- it is
   about the source reading consistently and about the next author not having
   to guess which one this file uses.

2. Task.pm documents `extra` with =attr and none of its other ~20 attributes
   (id, title, status, assignee, claimed_by, file_path, ...). That had a
   concrete cost during #118: three intended L</file_path> links had to be
   written as C<file_path> instead, because a link to an undocumented section
   is a podchecker error. So the gap is already shaping how neighbouring POD
   can be written.

Neither affects correctness. Both are the kind of thing that gets more
expensive the more POD accumulates around them.
